 ## Overview
-This method compresses a database of extracted cloud volumes by projecting their voxel density vectors onto a low-dimensional subspace defined by the left singular vectors of the dataset matrix. It differs from its parent, [PCA-based TSDF Compression](12932-pca-based-tsdf-compression.md), by operating directly on the raw voxel density values of normalized cloud blocks rather than on Signed Distance Field (SDF) or TSDF representations. While PCA relies on the covariance matrix of the data, this method explicitly constructs the data matrix and performs Singular Value Decomposition (SVD) to determine the basis, allowing for a direct energy-threshold-based truncation of the basis set.
+This method compresses a database of extracted cloud volumes by projecting their voxel density vectors onto a low-dimensional subspace defined by the left singular vectors of the dataset matrix [S1]. It differs from its parent, [PCA-based TSDF Compression](12932-pca-based-tsdf-compression.md), by operating directly on the raw voxel density values of normalized cloud blocks rather than on Signed Distance Field (SDF) or TSDF representations [S1]. While PCA relies on the covariance matrix of the data, this method explicitly constructs the data matrix and performs Singular Value Decomposition (SVD) to determine the basis, allowing for a direct threshold-based truncation of the basis set [S1].
 
